STEP 17
THINK have Undercarriage with two finished track loops around it (step 16). Bag 14 is open (it also holds loose hoses for later steps).
THINK goal Gives the machine a ring that lets the whole upper body swing round on the tracks.
THINK part sw-top-1 (88738 Technic Turntable Large Type 4 Top, 60 Tooth): black 60-tooth turntable top ring with three 3-hole blocks; spins
THINK part sw-base-1 (18939 Technic Turntable Large Type 3 Base): light-grey turntable base ring, snapped under the top ring; fixed
THINK part sw-bpin-1 (42924 Technic Pin Long with Friction Ridges Lengthwise, 1 Center Slot): four long blue pins pushed into the holes of the black blocks on the turntable top; fixed
THINK part sw-bpin-2 (42924 Technic Pin Long with Friction Ridges Lengthwise, 1 Center Slot): four long blue pins pushed into the holes of the black blocks on the turntable top; fixed
THINK part sw-bpin-3 (42924 Technic Pin Long with Friction Ridges Lengthwise, 1 Center Slot): four long blue pins pushed into the holes of the black blocks on the turntable top; fixed
THINK part sw-bpin-4 (42924 Technic Pin Long with Friction Ridges Lengthwise, 1 Center Slot): four long blue pins pushed into the holes of the black blocks on the turntable top; fixed
THINK touches Yellow box 1: the black turntable top is pressed onto the grey base ring. Yellow box 2: four blue pins go into the blocks on the top ring. The finished turntable is lowered onto the middle of the undercarriage (arrow) and the four grey pins (green arrows, two from each side) are pushed in through the base ring to lock it.
THINK does sw-top-1 spins on sw-base-1
THINK does uc-lpin-1 holds sw-base-1
THINK does uc-lpin-3 holds sw-base-1
THINK need slewing_ring: Lets a whole upper structure rotate on a base. Big turntables have teeth so a gear can drive the rotation. Rules: Base fixed to the chassis on at least two points; top carries everything above. The pinion's shaft must be fixed to the turning half so it walks round the ring.
THINK why A slewing ring (grey base + black top) is the Technic version of a real excavator's swing bearing; the four long pins already waiting in the frame lock the base without extra parts.
THINK role sw-top-1 in the swing turntable: Top half of the swing turntable: the upper machine is built on it and turns on it.
THINK role sw-base-1 in the swing turntable: Fixed half of the turntable, pinned to the undercarriage; holds the 60 teeth the top half runs on.
THINK role sw-bpin-1 in the swing turntable: Pin (42924) in the swing turntable.
THINK role sw-bpin-2 in the swing turntable: Pin (42924) in the swing turntable.
THINK role sw-bpin-3 in the swing turntable: Pin (42924) in the swing turntable.
THINK role sw-bpin-4 in the swing turntable: Pin (42924) in the swing turntable.
