STEP 18
THINK have Turntable on the undercarriage (step 17). The next steps build the pump deck in the air beside it (shown as a faded picture).
THINK goal Builds the air pump that will later power the arm's air cylinders.
THINK part pm-beam15-1 (32278 Technic Beam 1 x 15 Thick): two 15-hole dark-grey beams that carry the pump; fixed
THINK part pm-beam15-2 (32278 Technic Beam 1 x 15 Thick): two 15-hole dark-grey beams that carry the pump; fixed
THINK part pm-lpin-1 (42924 Technic Pin Long with Friction Ridges Lengthwise, 1 Center Slot): four long blue pins pushed into the first beam; fixed
THINK part pm-lpin-2 (42924 Technic Pin Long with Friction Ridges Lengthwise, 1 Center Slot): four long blue pins pushed into the first beam; fixed
THINK part pm-lpin-3 (42924 Technic Pin Long with Friction Ridges Lengthwise, 1 Center Slot): four long blue pins pushed into the first beam; fixed
THINK part pm-lpin-4 (42924 Technic Pin Long with Friction Ridges Lengthwise, 1 Center Slot): four long blue pins pushed into the first beam; fixed
THINK part pm-apin-1 (43093 Technic Axle Pin with Friction Ridges Lengthwise): one short blue axle pin; fixed
THINK part pm-hub-1 (44874 Technic Pin Connector Hub with 2 Pins with Friction Ridges Lengthwise [Small Squared Pin Holes]): black pin hub with two pins; fixed
THINK part pm-conn-1 (6536 Technic Axle and Pin Connector Perpendicular): black perpendicular axle-and-pin connector at the end of the beam; fixed
THINK part pm-hose-1 (5102c04 Hose, Pneumatic 4mm D. 4L / 3.2cm): short blue pneumatic hose (3.2 cm), length checked 1:1 on page 19; fixed
THINK part pm-pump-1 (26288 Pneumatic Pump Large (11L) with 1 x 3 Liftarm): blue pneumatic pump with black plunger top and a 1 x 3 base; moves up and down
THINK touches Sub-step 1: four blue long pins go into the first 15-hole beam, with a black connector at its far end. Sub-step 2: a black hub with a blue pin goes onto the beam (yellow box).
THINK touches Sub-step 3: the blue pump stands on three of the pins by its 1 x 3 base and the short blue hose is pushed onto its side nozzle (yellow box). Sub-step 4: the second 15-hole beam is pressed on under the pin ends. Page 20: the finished deck is placed on the turntable and the four blue pins of step 17 are pushed in from the sides (green arrows, two per side) to lock it.
THINK does pm-beam15-1 supports pm-pump-1
THINK does sw-bpin-1 holds pm-beam15-1
THINK does pm-lpin-2 holds pm-pump-1
THINK does pm-hose-1 carries pm-pump-1
THINK need pneumatic_circuit: A hand pump pushes air through hoses and switches into a cylinder; the cylinder rod pushes or pulls a part. Used where a real machine would use hydraulics. Rules: Every outlet that is used needs a hose pushed fully onto the nozzle. The cylinder must be pinned at both ends so its body and rod can swing. Unused nozzles must be capped or left closed, or air escapes.
THINK why A pump with a plunger pushed by hand pushes air through hoses; the two beams make a light frame for it.
THINK role pm-beam15-1 in the air system: Beam (32278) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role pm-beam15-2 in the air system: Beam (32278) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role pm-lpin-1 in the air system: Pin (42924) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role pm-lpin-2 in the air system: Pin (42924) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role pm-lpin-3 in the air system: Pin (42924) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role pm-lpin-4 in the air system: Pin (42924) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role pm-apin-1 in the air system: Pin (43093) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role pm-hub-1 in the air system: Pin (44874) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role pm-conn-1 in the air system: Connector (6536) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role pm-hose-1 in the air system: Air hose (5102c04) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role pm-pump-1 in the air system: Pneumatic pump (11L): pushing it makes air that the switches send to the cylinders.
