THINK need pneumatic_circuit: A hand pump pushes air through hoses and switches into a cylinder; the cylinder rod pushes or pulls a part. Used where a real machine would use hydraulics. Rules: Every outlet that is used needs a hose pushed fully onto the nozzle. The cylinder must be pinned at both ends so its body and rod can swing. Unused nozzles must be capped or left closed, or air escapes.
THINK why A T-piece splits the pump's air into two branches; a switch block on each branch lets the driver choose which cylinder moves.
THINK role hy-tee-1 in the air system: Air T-piece: splits one air line to two places.
THINK role hy-valve-1 in the air system: Pneumatic switch: a lever that chooses which way the air goes.
THINK role hy-valve-2 in the air system: Pneumatic switch: a second lever for the other cylinder.
THINK role hy-hose-1 in the air system: Air hose (5102c06) in the air (pneumatic) system.
THINK role hy-hose-2 in the air system: Air hose (5102c06) in the air (pneumatic) system.
