THINK need pneumatic_circuit: A hand pump pushes air through hoses and switches into a cylinder; the cylinder rod pushes or pulls a part. Used where a real machine would use hydraulics. Rules: Every outlet that is used needs a hose pushed fully onto the nozzle. The cylinder must be pinned at both ends so its body and rod can swing. Unused nozzles must be capped or left closed, or air escapes.
THINK need push_rod: A rod with a hinge at each end transfers push and pull between two parts that swing. Rules: Both ends must swing freely.
THINK why A cylinder pushing between two pivots turns the joint.
THINK role bm-cyl-1 in the arm and bucket: Air cylinder on the arm (step 90): pushes the lower arm at the elbow when air arrives.
THINK role bm-tpin-1 in the arm and bucket: Pin (39888) in the arm (boom, stick and bucket).
THINK role bm-tpin-2 in the arm and bucket: Pin (39888) in the arm (boom, stick and bucket).
